all right katie pavlich editor  townhall.com at a fox news contributor  katie good morning to you you know the  story well  uh you also know that probably in  american communities all over the  country they're having similar debates  how do you see this one  they are having similar debates and this  is a culmination of parents over the  past  year year and a half really being  ignored on national level  on the local level they've been fighting  teachers unions to get their kids back  in school  and now they're looking at these school  districts that are requiring little kids  to wear masks all day long despite the  science showing that might not be  necessary there's an interesting study  now out of brown university showing that  actually  mass mandates in schools k-12 schools  don't necessarily stop the spread of  this disease and so they're requiring  kids to do this and yesterday you had a  nurse  on the channel saying look she's she  sees these kids she's in new jersey and  there are injuries being inflicted on  these kids  from wearing masks for eight hours a day  they're getting blisters on their mouth  they're wearing dirty masks they're not  wearing them properly they're not being  switched out  the right way so there are other  consequences for this and to have the  school board allow politicians to take  the time away from the parents  who've been paying for all of this on a  number of different levels  is pretty egregious behavior dr scott  gottlieb had this to say about mass  i think we can do it right around now i  think we should start lifting these  restrictions  as i think we should start lifting these  restrictions as aggressively as we put  them in we need to preserve the  credibility of public health officials  to perhaps re-implement some of these  provisions as we get into next winter if  we  do start seeing outbreaks again i think  the only way to earn public credibility  is to demonstrate that you're willing to  relax these provisions when the  situation improves  uh dr gottlieb has been pretty um  forward-thinking on even at the  beginning of the virus he was like  everyone needs to take this very  seriously and now he's saying  that we're at a point when we can do  this do you think people might listen  i think people are listening i'm not  sure if the people at the cdc  are listening dr fauci for example with  these new cdc guidelines they put out  for  kids to be masked at summer camp when  they're outside and  while they're swimming and how you know  doing all these things that are contrary  to  what we know about the data of how this  disease spreads  outside and among younger children and  so  i think that you're going to see more  frustration from parents more  frustration from regular adults who are  saying look i got vaccinated  or maybe i didn't get vaccinated but we  know that the the disease is going away  and i shouldn't be shamed  or forced to continue acting like we're  in the middle of a pandemic last summer  when things have changed on the ground  so that incentive is certainly something  that  um should be given but the biden  administration hasn't shown any  you know willingness to change the  president wearing a mask  outside that's right i mean we saw them  in plains georgia early in the week with  the carters right  they were inside with them without a  mask took a picture came outside they  were wearing masks  we saw kamala harris on a tarmac early  week with her husband  they're both wearing masks and they kiss  before she gets on board the plane  i mean these confusing signals that it  doesn't encourage people to go ahead and  sign up for the vaccine how's your life  going to change that's what they're  asking  dr mark siegel wall street journal i  think that's a key point  end the mask mandate to spur vaccination  that's the case he makes he writes it's  your responsibility to protect yourself  by getting  your shots he concludes the message to  everyone vaccines work and it's time to  get back to normal so his plea  is to end the mandate on memorial  weekend which would be february  28th i don't know if that's something  president biden would do but it's an  interesting thought  in order to get encouragement out there  well look the federal government and  governments and local school districts  continue to make this argument  that these these restrictions are  necessary because it gives them an  argument on the other side to say what  they need to do in order to  fix the problem whether it's more  government spending or especially among  the teachers unions they want more money  to you know make their their schools  safer as they try to argue  but the bottom line is that the american  people have been very patient they have  been very compliant when it comes to  trying to get through this pandemic in  the right way possible and they have  seen a number of mixed signals  from people like dr fauci from the white  house  from guidelines that were given last  summer about how to move forward with  this and so when dr gottlieb says this  is about credibility  for health officials now it is because  people are saying  well i've done everything i'm supposed  to do and yet i still can't go back to  acting like i'm  i'm in my normal life again despite  doing everything i've been told and so  that is not something that bodes well  for the future  if there were another health crisis in  terms of people listening to  those guidelines since they've been  changed so often  very interesting to hear from those  parents i mean they're fighting for the  kids  that was clear in that video we heard  from sultan thank you katie nice to see  you  have a good friday

